# Canonical author identity for this repository.
#
# This repository is research data for a PhD on human oversight in agentic
# software development. Analysis attributes every oversight episode to the
# human who caught it, so each author must resolve to exactly one identity
# regardless of which machine or git config produced the commit.
#
# .mailmap only changes how names are DISPLAYED (git log, git shortlog,
# git blame). It rewrites nothing. The commits themselves are untouched.
#
# Verify after any change:
#     git shortlog -sne --all     # should list one line per real person
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> Commit Name <commit@email>
#
# As of 22 September 2026, `git shortlog -sne --all` reports exactly one
# identity across all history, so there are no variants to fold in yet. The
# line below fixes that identity as canonical; add a mapping line for each
# new variant as it appears (a different machine, a work email, a changed
# display name).

srimalhs <srimalhs@gmail.com>
